.com/repos/saltcorn/react/commits/c615f2056365443c776165ac5d84ca70ad24e7c4"}],"sha":"83030c3dec63af3e79a74996b1ec204cf2fc8180","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saltcorn/react/commits/83030c3dec63af3e79a74996b1ec204cf2fc8180"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10777655?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christianhugoch/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christianhugoch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christianhugoch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christianhugoch/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/christianhugoch","id":10777655,"login":"christianhugoch","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNzc3NjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christianhugoch/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christianhugoch/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christianhugoch/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christianhugoch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christianhugoch/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/christianhugoch","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saltcorn/react/commits/c615f2056365443c776165ac5d84ca70ad24e7c4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-04-08T13:00:21Z","email":"hugo.christian@web.de","name":"christianhugoch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-04-08T13:00:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"split into global-main and view bundle (#10)\n\n* split into global-main and view bundle\n- main bundle has React, ReactDOM + a user components lib\n    comes from the plugin cfg menu\n- view bundle has shared access to main\n    comes from a code_editor in the view cfg menu\n\n* not set code-source-type, corrected help and README\n\n* basic-structure example, helper functions from the main bundle\n- show how to export React components from your user-lib and use react-lib\n- import user-lib in the main bundle, then there is no need to lazy load them later,\n  but it''s still possible (added react-lazily to make it easier)\n\n* example with react-router\n- in your user-lib directory define react-router-dom as normal dependency\n- dependencies that are already in main_bundle can go into peerDeps\n\n* expose generic everything from the user-lib for consumers\n\n* the main bundle loads remotes at runtime with @module-federation/runtime\n- view bundles (remote from the perspective of main) are loaded at runtime when needed\n- no circular deps when building main\n- and we don''t have to know all React views when building main\n\n* no App.js name conflict, simplified build_view script params\n- use viewname for ModuleFederationPlugin exposes property\n  - a fixed value causes trouble with multiple views:\n    it takes the first loaded remote and maps everything to this module\n- write user-code into ${viewname}.js\n- viewnames with whitespaces will propably cause trouble for now\n\n* removed old user-code","tree":{"sha":"75742b35f0738ee9af45dbacd4ca532826359a51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saltcorn/react/git/trees/75742b35f0738ee9af45dbacd4ca532826359a51"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saltcorn/react/git/commits/c615f2056365443c776165ac5d84ca70ad24e7c4","verification":{"payload":"tree 75742b35f0738ee9af45dbacd4ca532826359a51\nparent d48c3f35149290f8cf76281f7aa5906bb2820856\nauthor christianhugoch <hugo.christian@web.de> 1744117221 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1744117221 +0200\n\nsplit into global-main and view bundle (#10)\n\n* split into global-main and view bundle\n- main bundle has React, ReactDOM + a user components lib\n    comes from the plugin cfg menu\n- view bundle has shared access to main\n    comes from a code_editor in the view cfg menu\n\n* not set code-source-type, corrected help and README\n\n* basic-structure example, helper functions from the main bundle\n- show how to export React components from your user-lib and use react-lib\n- import user-lib in the main bundle, then there is no need to lazy load them later,\n  but it''s still possible (added react-lazily to make it easier)\n\n* example with react-router\n- in your user-lib directory define react-router-dom as normal dependency\n- dependencies that are already in main_bundle can go into peerDeps\n\n* expose generic everything from the user-lib for consumers\n\n* the main bundle loads remotes at runtime with @module-federation/runtime\n- view bundles (remote from the perspective of main) are loaded at runtime when needed\n- no circular deps when building main\n- and we don''t have to know all React views when building main\n\n* no App.js name conflict, simplified build_view script params\n- use viewname for ModuleFederationPlugin exposes property\n  - a fixed value causes trouble with multiple views:\n    it takes the first loaded remote and maps everything to this module\n- write user-code into ${viewname}.js\n- viewnames with whitespaces will propably cause trouble for now\n\n* removed old user-code","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJn9R3lCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtC0QAEBo6GvCT7FBvhG2C/KsXVHO\n43Z9jZLSb1V2OXsCnxw5Idvgca1ksfSR/DfzlxsuhaTwMJTJZPB65Ay5Q9qnjFhp\nna09skb+tzKMOH0PpFRD+TLy3FnkCjW5mLHSHwbSYfshpnMKI9cA46FG9kC0aV8K\no6eOeu03ky9p82zixX5X8Ba+f8XT+GYU2md+G3vDd1FH4gxQ7T0v7Cp8HIpSZfZX\ntiCMxfet1pAZ8TFW3X75/1v1/FUQMJ+tZJhl9/c6zalEAYv7Q4nC0MtsAxOuquyH\nor59GH9Vooe8DVlnKnLudLOB/cMaPwPL5z33kqeshUhrcDJFcCZTmQADmJUs2ee1\ndrdc/ac64vUTEKHz2pMjqNLnma79GkeLSfpYtcSHkH/FXoB04Iu1bOosghGXoj3v\n7bgWXs13Oo+F/1sOl0J31ybyoPCsvfw9YYf71/4vOQbBNK44dYHqfiLklNwImuYU\nu/LHfFbANW5HFO2NRJ3U6wsqVvbalH2UF6QXK4+PR+wJP106Va+19GX6KC3Saa7k\nf0E2aCqkSsAYG0pLEitigSjEMYTU60Qjlzs0vH8ZviDVOaXdCQpF5v0NtbeQjI7q\nO/KHff5cPRbSrnRw/lt0wdNiaWVgDsoj8AsOLmub53yc9l8OCjNNB2w1Ye4/lD/I\nQKwGrTVDXUOA/hAhXw7k\n=Vhyu\n-----END PGP SIGNA