comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/evenflow58/40kauspex/commits/38f40bbd6d41e5130b23680c34c1a03ec4da45e1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T22:51:27Z","email":"evenflow58@gmail.com","name":"evenflow58"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T22:51:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(testing): add unit and E2E tests for all three companion pages and shared views (#22)\n\nUnit tests for GameSelectionPage, ArmyBuilderPage, PhaseCompanionPage, and\nStatusViews were entirely absent; the only coverage was a surface-level route\ncheck in App.test.tsx. The new tests cover loading/error states, user\ninteractions (faction selection, unit add/remove, phase navigation), save-flow\nnavigation, and retry logic — 39 net-new assertions.\n\nE2E authenticated suite expanded from one smoke check to six tests that\nverify the shell structure, primary nav, Companion routing, and game-selection\nheading. Smoke suite gains a /games API test alongside the existing /health check.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"62030df9de211fcec499ceca6ddd4c558473706d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/evenflow58/40kauspex/git/trees/62030df9de211fcec499ceca6ddd4c558473706d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/evenflow58/40kauspex/git/commits/38f40bbd6d41e5130b23680c34c1a03ec4da45e1","verification":{"payload":"tree 62030df9de211fcec499ceca6ddd4c558473706d\nparent 36665d6337be4d618e9bdc8372b0d5223784f81c\nauthor evenflow58 <evenflow58@gmail.com> 1780181487 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780181487 -0400\n\nfeat(testing): add unit and E2E tests for all three companion pages and shared views (#22)\n\nUnit tests for GameSelectionPage, ArmyBuilderPage, PhaseCompanionPage, and\nStatusViews were entirely absent; the only coverage was a surface-level route\ncheck in App.test.tsx. The new tests cover loading/error states, user\ninteractions (faction selection, unit add/remove, phase navigation), save-flow\nnavigation, and retry logic — 39 net-new assertions.\n\nE2E authenticated suite expanded from one smoke check to six tests that\nverify the shell structure, primary nav, Companion routing, and game-selection\nheading. Smoke suite gains a /games API test alongside the existing /health check.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqG2nvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOwgQADyb8TnQyz2K8lz3RGcZB/Yk\nUuMP3zOSZ1acBPXNmKnZLzn1ZxS+Kfrh622etXc5rjsII+EmXHI+iIctyGGx0/Em\nRfA8+GcvNtroAeeDxWsCON6C1e/wdxw94A25aspyssN59RZdpTMT7r2aSTuJ5yNj\n3enTQExcypBcjorqY/ASYRb88QpxpbT/99uR31pJj94rqblCQXZEgPxyPar9CarX\nPBndPR4I7zU9mYdiFzKjoluS4swaAg4NYMHWhPMEPd7c3D6QVtK/ym+KPWQMBeqn\nfope6nKipNVpU7RVsBvLsCUXoyXyW6iq46PZAcRpsRZVkuHeHe34Dnn7sqS5mnDQ\nvkUeeFsJJtytOYAtqekVIurbxbNUTANUFq79r5/Wh+t5MP+uk+H18C0c24nqfxP1\noZFYYc6SaMEpNkb3VEXrkdkqSURb+nfxAleB9bY4HaerOmzAduBCidqlQvX/+AtO\nSMg8/+VNf6KkQuRhDxaZWWEYVSC67avZtoQnYS+vEQh4qUFvhLH88TCGcOa+KgXP\nyJ6sPmZ8oImg1lQA7A6wrOTyWhBrqKZtfWm024mh+iEiZwbs0MEYoUCk7ILXwQyx\nYvE/CrOpiHcwstsmEA1Im/vI7GniMUdiWj8i928WPnruAVl/j8qpWGn9/+G83+xT\nGzLNgbqrWLf3wzkuVsS1\n=2Z0T\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-30T22:51:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/evenflow58/40kauspex/commit/38f40bbd6d41e5130b23680c34c1a03ec4da45e1","node_id":"C_kwDOOFd91doAKDM4ZjQwYmJkNmQ0MWU1MTMwYjIzNjgwYzM0YzFhMDNlYzRkYTQ1ZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/evenflow58/40kauspex/commit/36665d6337be4d618e9bdc8372b0d5223784f81c","sha":"36665d6337be4d618e9bdc8372b0d5223784f81c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/evenflow58/40kauspex/commits/36665d6337be4d618e9bdc8372b0d5223784f81c"}],"sha":"38f40bbd6d41e5130b23680c34c1a03ec4da45e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/evenflow58/40kauspex/commits/38f40bbd6d41e5130b23680c34c1a03ec4da45e1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11801612?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/evenflow58","id":11801612,"login":"evenflow58","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExODAxNjEy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/evenflow58/40kauspex/commits/36665d6337be4d618e9bdc8372b0d5223784f81c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T20:11:31Z","email":"evenflow58@gmail.com","name":"evenflow58"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T20:11:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(testing): add Pact consumer-driven contract tests for all three API services (#21)\n\nConsumer tests in mfe-companion define the expected request/response\nshapes for all 10 API endpoints and generate pact files to pacts/.\nProvider verification tests in each Lambda service start a minimal\nHTTP server wrapping the real handler (with mocked DynamoDB) and run\nthe Pact verifier against the generated contracts.\n\nFixes from code review:\n- Remove briefAbility: nullValue() — Pact V3 has no nullable matcher;\n  omitting the field avoids a false ''must be null'' constraint on a\n  string|null field\n- Use dynamic ports (listen(0)) instead of hardcoded 19001-19003 to\n  prevent EADDRINUSE flakiness in concurrent CI runs\n- Pass actual HTTP method through buildEvent in the armies provider\n  so the event is correct for POST/PUT/DELETE interactions\n- Wire pnpm test:pact into the CI deploy workflow so contracts are\n  verified on every PR\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cf00b09d3309d17aeaa27a3d284112b42cb5662b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/evenflow58/40kauspex/git/trees/cf00b09d3309d17aeaa27a3d284112b42cb5662b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/evenflow58/40kauspex/git/commits/36665d6337be4d618e9bdc8372b0d5223784f81c","verification":{"payload":"tree cf00b09d3309d17aeaa27a3d284112b42cb5662b\nparent ad784de4d645e4810f475b2f71672adfd11337b0\nauthor evenflow58 <evenflow58@gmail.com> 1780171891 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780171891 -0400\n\nfeat(testing): add Pact consumer-driven contract tests for all three API services (#21)\n\nConsumer tests in mfe-companion define the expected request/response\nshapes for all 10 API endpoints and generate pact files to pacts/.\nProvider verification tests in each Lambda service start a minimal\nHTTP server wrapping the real handler (with mocked DynamoDB) and run\nthe Pact verifier against the generated contracts.\n\nFixes from code review:\n- Remove briefAbility: nullValue() — Pact V3 has no nullable matcher;\n  omitting the field avoids a false ''must be null'' constraint on a\n  string|null field\n- Use dynamic ports (listen(0)) instead of hardcoded 19001-19003 to\n  prevent EADDRINUSE flakiness in concurrent CI runs\n- Pass actual HTTP method through buildEvent in the armies provider\n  so the event is correct for POST/PUT/DELETE interactions\n- Wire pnpm test:pact into the CI deploy workflow so contracts are\n  verified on every PR\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqG0RzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmx0QACcRbit4iozW8E/982BFHB+V\naYtUqkjliQjGRJUfFAMRalFl/GgKJijZiIYHFY6Q0bilfFnCxVNT/Rv4fI2ouERU\nmVSy0jeE/u61g97eGlZNRa77VYZb5JZhww+4rK9OkOWi6Fy/AUP54g1SFHsOZU8T\n7TYWOsnn/3NBT7QKah1g50qlvdM0V4xcfCkGhyLOZGqq4pB+C12pGU0II8BUcH4O\n940prRnCUYjLp+LNMVQ/vSnR4g27JqEcyQBy+m2Bj21lOJHSs+uo6+EkfHVY/CBg\n2gufoOs+qKZ7Vkoa0XsrgG5lG2QIsCF0dzAvwbTCssHqy8lOpI6ea/0QFyMzOErI\nqzIE/pe0trLC9rX/bF4RQR8WE/wkR57FfWACuRCWUllGWZ/2/UA21xSrkkcLb8z0\nuHsOfCSzuKe+OAoQ6TlSSB1bdA9AegviQGBbMKG5HVKVisn+mA0tUx7MAYvBM6Xl\nwzxkE/6o9okOtbATfCSTpsRHIXgR+WoE/q3G7kh3zPzDlU3I7NNTAx34xaGnUlv/\nrfdZmEAQWW45/uBDdBnTEaxMisUEhJk83M+uZeqkEW/nTK5krxj7D9VW/5O+A+Tc\nkFyxfXNmxd4kbUjzD4LH1+PC5hLWGaHy+9nielaAR6x1XObqfP6+MiU13BnYnjv6\nNrToqePdIbgU831F8Sli\n=A3R2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-30T20:11:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.