_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/evenflow58/40kauspex/commits/13819dd5beba24fb2a478035f744facdd66e320b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T14:17:31Z","email":"evenflow58@gmail.com","name":"evenflow58"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T14:17:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(shell): wire mfe-companion into shell with primary nav and routing (#19)\n\n* feat(shell): wire mfe-companion into shell with primary nav and routing\n\nAdds a Nav component (Home / Companion links) to the shell header and\nroutes /companion/* to the mfe-companion remote via Module Federation.\nShares react-router-dom as a singleton across all MFEs so remote <Routes>\nparticipate in the shell''s <BrowserRouter>. Removes the companion catch-all\nroute — unknown paths now render nothing rather than silently redirecting.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(infra): add mfe-companion CloudFront behaviour and S3 sync\n\nAdds /mfe-companion/* behaviour to the CloudFront distribution (mirrors\nmfe-home: no SPA rewrite, CORS headers, optimised caching) and syncs\napps/mfe-companion/dist to the S3 bucket in the PR ephemeral deploy\nworkflow. The production pipeline already included the mfe-companion sync.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: restore pnpm-lock.yaml entries lost during rebase\n\nThe rebase merge of pnpm-lock.yaml dropped the packages/lambda-utils\nimporter section and its workspace:* references in services/armies and\nservices/phase-guide. Regenerated with pnpm install.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"045f169e6008a36fb106c135d9caad79c3d23b81","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/evenflow58/40kauspex/git/trees/045f169e6008a36fb106c135d9caad79c3d23b81"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/evenflow58/40kauspex/git/commits/13819dd5beba24fb2a478035f744facdd66e320b","verification":{"payload":"tree 045f169e6008a36fb106c135d9caad79c3d23b81\nparent f3db65a1ec199791c4cbf763b80821a64f73371f\nauthor evenflow58 <evenflow58@gmail.com> 1780150651 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780150651 -0400\n\nfeat(shell): wire mfe-companion into shell with primary nav and routing (#19)\n\n* feat(shell): wire mfe-companion into shell with primary nav and routing\n\nAdds a Nav component (Home / Companion links) to the shell header and\nroutes /companion/* to the mfe-companion remote via Module Federation.\nShares react-router-dom as a singleton across all MFEs so remote <Routes>\nparticipate in the shell''s <BrowserRouter>. Removes the companion catch-all\nroute — unknown paths now render nothing rather than silently redirecting.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(infra): add mfe-companion CloudFront behaviour and S3 sync\n\nAdds /mfe-companion/* behaviour to the CloudFront distribution (mirrors\nmfe-home: no SPA rewrite, CORS headers, optimised caching) and syncs\napps/mfe-companion/dist to the S3 bucket in the PR ephemeral deploy\nworkflow. The production pipeline already included the mfe-companion sync.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: restore pnpm-lock.yaml entries lost during rebase\n\nThe rebase merge of pnpm-lock.yaml dropped the packages/lambda-utils\nimporter section and its workspace:* references in services/armies and\nservices/phase-guide. Regenerated with pnpm install.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGvF7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGE8QAHU4AsDbJfT+jhCLjf1OtEjm\nHgp9ByZhKgr+Q6fgWDSzNRF+sOAFQwjn+NgcnXfXxJVw7kq/w84y1oEE/I935tx1\nYpehkKPXiqeyi4ufWq7PBpHb4MdGLV/18/oUt71vVnikNl66helPNsLQwCoPNFwv\nS140e/UeXOcywAm89mDy9Y5XBROL+0ZnMifDHXYHx97HrW9VGKd