subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/evenflow58/40kauspex/commit/f3db65a1ec199791c4cbf763b80821a64f73371f","node_id":"C_kwDOOFd91doAKGYzZGI2NWExZWMxOTk3OTFjNGNiZjc2M2I4MDgyMWE2NGY3MzM3MWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/evenflow58/40kauspex/commit/8019379edb50ba057e5ea35e0babf4a24a7f605a","sha":"8019379edb50ba057e5ea35e0babf4a24a7f605a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/evenflow58/40kauspex/commits/8019379edb50ba057e5ea35e0babf4a24a7f605a"}],"sha":"f3db65a1ec199791c4cbf763b80821a64f73371f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/evenflow58/40kauspex/commits/f3db65a1ec199791c4cbf763b80821a64f73371f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11801612?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/evenflow58","id":11801612,"login":"evenflow58","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExODAxNjEy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/evenflow58/40kauspex/commits/8019379edb50ba057e5ea35e0babf4a24a7f605a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T11:55:17Z","email":"evenflow58@gmail.com","name":"evenflow58"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T11:55:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(companion): wire mfe-companion into the shell (#15)\n\n* feat(companion): add games reference-data Lambda service\n\nGET /games, /games/{gameId}/phases, /games/{gameId}/factions, and\n/factions/{factionId}/units — public endpoints that serve read-only\ngame catalogue data from DynamoDB. Includes a custom-resource seeder\n(seed.ts) that populates the table with Warhammer 40K v10 core data\non first deploy.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(companion): add armies CRUD Lambda service\n\nJWT-authenticated endpoints (POST/GET/PUT/DELETE /armies) for managing\na user''s saved armies. Each army stores a faction selection and a list\nof units. Uses the same DynamoDB table via the single-table design:\nPK=USER#<sub>, SK=ARMY#<armyId> and PK=ARMY#<armyId>, SK=UNIT#<...>.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(companion): add phase-guide Lambda service\n\nJWT-authenticated GET /phase-guide?game=<id>&phase=<order> that\nreturns structured guidance for the active game phase (objective,\nallowed actions, key rules). Data lives in DynamoDB alongside the\ngame catalogue so no extra table is needed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(companion): scaffold mfe-companion micro-frontend\n\nNew Module-Federation remote on port 3002. Sets up Vite + React +\nTailwind + vite-plugin-federation with the bootstrap/main entry-point\nsplit needed for async imports. Module type declarations added so\nTypeScript resolves the remote module at compile time.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(companion): wire mfe-companion into the shell\n\n- MainLayout: add /companion/* route that lazy-loads mfe-companion via\n  Module Federation\n- vite.config.ts: register mfe-companion as a federation remote at\n  /mfe-companion/assets/remoteEntry.js\n- declarations.d.ts: add mfe_companion/App type declaration\n- mfe-companion-stub.tsx: test stub so shell unit tests run without the\n  remote MFE being available\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"512d38ae6ab7faf9c8f3e528562aaef59f1e7581","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/evenflow58/40kauspex/git/trees/512d38ae6ab7faf9c8f3e528562aaef59f1e7581"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/evenflow58/40kauspex/git/commits/8019379edb50ba057e5ea35e0babf4a24a7f605a","verification":{"payload":"tree 512d38ae6ab7faf9c8f3e528562aaef59f1e7581\nparent 5a196521add485229f55bc595ec5dd3424134624\nauthor evenflow58 <evenflow58@gmail.com> 1780142117 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780142117 -0400\n\nfeat(companion): wire mfe-companion into the shell (#15)\n\n* feat(companion): add games reference-data Lambda service\n\nGET /games, /games/{gameId}/phases, /games/{gameId}/factions, and\n/factions/{factionId}/units — public endpoints that serve read-only\ngame catalogue data from DynamoDB. Includes a custom-resource seeder\n(seed.ts) that populates the table with Warhammer 40K v10 core data\non first deploy.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(companion): add armies CRUD Lambda service\n\nJWT-authenticated endpoints (POST/GET/PUT/DELETE /armies) for managing\na user''s saved armies. Each army stores a faction selection and a list\nof units. Uses the same DynamoDB table via the single-table design:\nPK=USER#<sub>, SK=ARMY#<armyId> and PK=ARMY#<armyId>, SK=UNIT#<...>.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(companion): add phase-guide Lambda service\n\nJWT-authenticated GET /phase-guide?game=<id>&phase=<order> that\nreturns structured guidance for the active game phase (objective,\nallowed actions, key rules). Data lives in DynamoDB alongside the\ngame catalogue so no extra table is needed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(companion): scaffold mfe-companion micro-frontend\n\nNew Module-Federation remote on port 3002. Sets up Vite + React +\nTailwind + vite-plugin-federation with the bootstrap/main entry-point\nsplit needed for async imports. Module type declarations added so\nTypeScript resolves the remote module at compile time.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(companion): wire mfe-companion into the shell\n\n- MainLayout: add /companion/* route that lazy-loads mfe-companion via\n  Module Federation\n- vite.config.ts: register mfe-companion as a federation remote at\n  /mfe-companion/assets/remoteEntry.js\n- declarations.d.ts: add mfe_companion/App type declaration\n- mfe-companion-stub.tsx: test stub so shell unit tests run without the\n  remote MFE being available\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGtAlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzpQQACYGmHTaPhfm0AYL+TlC2Yvd\nJVrHn/6A+P+K8wlJGir2Cm4p1bdSBrj66Jq9SEC4ao/BnmwFOkeVBhzaZg7JvNte\nf+3b5YYOXU1PxHmA9rSFuB4vIytSU93m8r7BIw9MigifB0YehIXUPTS6wxgMz7H1\nutjNV+nISF759Q7IASadl7jGnYK4/JcrZhoplx2pG/z4rHsM0EvDtcCVHDbq8RH7\nLjrhNq1SAW6Gftp5lktLtW8oS/WFK0jOi4dgshQaanScWBrOGA/CeaKfjExUSqgV\nGgNSguBSCbpQbEGnTjgoz0t0FkuWTiqEFVfPsVL4BSTw9EChd/wq359AQE0AYP1Y\nxh1mV0tn3wYB9ENKzL3x+po0xkBYjP+lEy0mfDhaZPrivTSmi2x9KPP+hcFotBf3\ncB4h3iOc39pdsmtEWaYDCPZLhHCDujc7kBitbZJSQIflCpJjYYkWOsXCh62rx8gr\noHPla3Z66McKqZ7ovh24Os7/f0dzzkHsVzcuZAd3fa8QBU3AETcmjBS+6GPR9CR3\nIbPBFkwsiM35q64E4mOMfEP8B5qRgLSJK9yoGM991ndJB+U7cA5cZSOaCGlop/8y\nLiBowmo/Q3YOhVvaB24XTAbSv3h3m50rrQJu/HgKGdWmPpXheI+sTvkAlcS0mgWI\n+xHx8pvUepgSMa7LeiQt\n=qkgD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-30T11:55:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/evenflow58/40kauspex/commit/8019379edb50ba057e5ea35e0babf4a24a7f605a","node_id":"C_kwDOOFd91doAKDgwMTkzNzllZGI1MGJhMDU3ZTVlYTM1ZTBiYWJmNGEyNGE3ZjYwNWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/evenflow58/40kauspex/commit/5a196521add485229f55bc595ec5dd3424134624","sha":"5a196521add485229f55bc595ec5dd3424134624","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/evenflow58/40kauspex/commits/5a196521add485229f55bc595ec5dd3424134624"}],"sha":"8019379edb50ba057e5ea35e0babf4a24a7f605a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/evenflow58/40kauspex/commits/8019379edb50ba057e5ea35e0babf4a24a7f605a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11801612?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/evenflow58","id":11801612,"login":"evenflow58","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExODAxNjEy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/evenflow58","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/evenflow58/40kauspex/commits/5a196521add485229f55bc595ec5dd3424134624/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-25T13:38:34Z","email":"evenflow58@gmail.com","name":"evenflow58"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-25T13:38:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(companion): add game selection, army builder, and phase companion pages (#14)\n\n* feat(companion): add DataStack, companion API routes, and pipeline sync\n\n- data-stack.ts: new DynamoDB single-table construct for companion data\n- api-stack.ts: add /games, /factions, /phases, /units and JWT-authed\n  /armies + /phase-guide routes\n- app-stage.ts: wire DataStack into the stage and export its outputs\n- bin/infrastructure.ts: register DataStack in the CDK app\n- pipeline-stack.ts: add mfe-companion dist sync and E2E test step\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(companion): add games reference-data Lambda service\n\nGET /games, /games/{gameId}/phases, /games/{gameId}/factions, and\n/factions/{factionId}/units — public endpoints that serve read-only\ngame catalogue data from DynamoDB. Includes a custom-resource seeder\n(seed.ts) that populates the table with Warhammer 40K v10 core data\non first deploy.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(companion): add armies CRUD Lambda service\n\nJWT-authenticated endpoints (POST/GET/PUT/DELETE /armies) for managing\na user''s saved armies. Each army stores a faction selection and a list\nof units. Uses the same DynamoDB table via the single-table design:\nPK=USER#<sub>, SK=ARMY#<armyId> and PK=ARMY#<armyId>, SK=UNIT#<...>.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(companion): add phase-guide Lambda service\n\nJWT-authenticated GET /phase-guide?game=<id>&phase=<order> that\nreturns structured guidance for the active game phase (objective,\nallowed actions, key rules). Data lives in DynamoDB alongside the\ngame catalogue so no extra table is needed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(companion): scaffold mfe-companion micro-frontend\n\nNew Module-Federation remote on port 3002. Sets up Vite + React +\nTailwind + vite-plugin-federation with the bootstrap/main entry-point\nsplit needed for async imports. Module type declarations added so\nTypeScript resolves the remote module at compile time.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(companion): add game selection, army builder, and phase companion pages\n\nThree-screen companion flow:\n- GameSelectionPage: list available games, persist choice to sessionStorage\n- ArmyBuilderPage: pick a faction and add/remove units; army saved to the\n  armies service via JWT-authed API calls\n- PhaseCompanionPage: tabbed 5-phase tracker with active-phase highlight\n  and guidance text from the phase-guide service\n\nIncludes shared StatusViews component (Loading/Error/Empty) and the\napi.ts client that wires all three pages to the backend.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add memory for amended commits\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cd70e14c7005f6e2b0e951942a4993cbb26ccac7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/evenflow58/40kauspex/git/trees/cd70e14c7005f6e2b0e951942a4993cbb26ccac7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/evenflow58/40kauspex/git/commits/5a196521add485229f55bc595ec5dd3424134624","verification":{"payload":"tree cd70e14c7005f6e2b0e951942a4993cbb26ccac7\nparent 2c1d31725c80a2206d7d1d69653adf418df7ed41\nauthor evenflow58 <evenflow58@gmail.com> 1779716314 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779716314 -0400\n\nfeat(companion): add game selection, army builder, and phase companion pages (#14)\n\n* feat(companion): add DataStack, companion API routes, and pipeline sync\n\n- data-stack.ts: new DynamoDB single-table construct for companion data\n- api-stack.ts: add /games, /factions, /phases, /units and JWT-authed\n  /armies + /phase-guide routes\n- app-stage.ts: wire DataStack into the stage and export its outputs\n- bin/infrastructure.ts: register DataStack in the CDK app\n- pipeline-stack.ts: add mfe-companion dist sync and E2E test step\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(companion): add games reference-data Lambda service\n\nGET /games, /games/{gameId}/phases, /games/{gameId}/factions, and\n/factions/{factionId}/units — public endpoints that serve read-only\ngame catalogue data from DynamoDB. Includes a custom-resource seeder\n(seed.ts) that populates the table with Warhammer 40K v10 core data\non first deploy.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(companion): add armies CRUD Lambda service\n\nJWT-authenticated endpoints (POST/GET/PUT/DELETE /armies) for managing\na user''s saved armies. Each army stores a faction selection and a list\nof units. Uses the same DynamoDB table via the single-table design:\nPK=USER#<sub>, SK=ARMY#<armyId> and PK=ARMY#<armyId>, SK=UNIT#<...>.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(companion): add phase-guide Lambda service\n\nJWT-authenticated GET /phase-guide?game=<id>&phase=<order> that\nreturns structured guidance for the active game phase (objective,\nallowed actions, key rules). Data lives in DynamoDB alongside the\ngame catalogue so no extra table is needed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(companion): scaffold mfe-companion micro-frontend\n\nNew Module-Federation remote on port 3002. Sets up Vite + React +\nTailwind + vite-plugin-federation with the bootstrap/main entry-point\nsplit needed for async imports. Module type declarations added so\nTypeScript resolves the remote module at compile time.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(companion): add game selection, army builder, and phase companion pages\n\nThree-screen companion flow:\n- GameSelectionPage: list available games, persist choice to sessionStorage\n- ArmyBuilderPage: pick a faction and add/remove units; army saved to the\n  armies service via JWT-authed API calls\n- PhaseCompanionPage: tabbed 5-phase tracker with active-phase highlight\n  and guidance text from the phase-guide service\n\nIncludes shared StatusViews component (Loading/Error/Empty) and the\napi.ts client that wires all three pages to the backend.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add memory for amended commits\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqFFDaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzboQABlQI7ATiVG83rAA6T/0HGzH\nRjo8DiXYRd8XD5SkQSmGJKpzu4+kye5iAtOxzsXHvkWgzvulRDQRNsi6U2RLo3fq\nBLGsUL4WmyblBvLFlh7GdveMXN37qO5Y0K6peTfEnT2jCMJlUfW8Gk672sByTNsU\nja8FPBV309qvYShiT6o87mSovQ4ZPcLrTc5mrcih4t5TIfdtS69wXrP2C4NZRhkX\njqeLcp2vyC8ULGRPJkI4abU2h2YLXRMmyR7SyO3rj6X2jmiELMe7dLHes0KH9Ehh\n3ZAAPJfCq2KkVfg/AgXlPdzjWPKsbn7CiFsXccFdR9FoGrRixZUXcztOY/oS25in\ni+ihU83hc1MwRnCRX1EveKGumO1uXeg+gdvk2oT2X0VCePI7caMG4CEKRUZC3n3q\nOP91qaYzl2nLAGgZL1q1gTuEDwgZqrjrUrNsOiFQuG6tBLAD1kxR76SuaMz6IWlg\nTt5qTL/mfI63qEuFPofSFs7fftbziEbSv576BXT+U4nQkb+hATYBETp2vH1OrE++\n8LK9jit/8fuzvj8wirnm5488uhgCHg6hzAImNvFwdeqm/+RT0q5NjrHgOn9R7Yt6\n7uFY5mx5G68UkG37Tc+SjYI5qslZNlMalFxmdcHDSTqEpjs+LA4OjF+L7rIJ+Gpv\nNxW+Vtlv+xy/jqV/LoVs\n=Xrrn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-25T13:38:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubuserconte