companion dist sync and E2E test step\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(companion): add games reference-data Lambda service\n\nGET /games, /games/{gameId}/phases, /games/{gameId}/factions, and\n/factions/{factionId}/units — public endpoints that serve read-only\ngame catalogue data from DynamoDB. Includes a custom-resource seeder\n(seed.ts) that populates the table with Warhammer 40K v10 core data\non first deploy.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(companion): add armies CRUD Lambda service\n\nJWT-authenticated endpoints (POST/GET/PUT/DELETE /armies) for managing\na user''s saved armies. Each army stores a faction selection and a list\nof units. Uses the same DynamoDB table via the single-table design:\nPK=USER#<sub>, SK=ARMY#<armyId> and PK=ARMY#<armyId>, SK=UNIT#<...>.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(companion): add phase-guide Lambda service\n\nJWT-authenticated GET /phase-guide?game=<id>&phase=<order> that\nreturns structured guidance for the active game phase (objective,\nallowed actions, key rules). Data lives in DynamoDB alongside the\ngame catalogue so no extra table is needed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e0bfa9e98dfd6cf45afb92ecf1c4de4fb220ba42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/evenflow58/40kauspex/git/trees/e0bfa9e98dfd6cf45afb92ecf1c4de4fb220ba42"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/evenflow58/40kauspex/git/commits/62f5e1a8bae4f746b3f60c63bcd4d5a8237abac8","verification":{"payload":"tree e0bfa9e98dfd6cf45afb92ecf1c4de4fb220ba42\nparent 96db4ff8f5e29ffbb302a38593fa74cdb0b97b65\nauthor evenflow58 <evenflow58@gmail.com> 1779647478 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779647478 -0400\n\nfeat(companion): add phase-guide Lambda service (#12)\n\n* feat(companion): add DataStack, companion API routes, and pipeline sync