/commit/3d5bc276dbbc2991a99bbbce64916001f4f58d35","sha":"3d5bc276dbbc2991a99bbbce64916001f4f58d35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chaotic-art/app/commits/3d5bc276dbbc2991a99bbbce64916001f4f58d35"}],"sha":"7a9994c49e36bc0ce9791d6a350a745db5ae2b2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chaotic-art/app/commits/7a9994c49e36bc0ce9791d6a350a745db5ae2b2d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/734428?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/preschian/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/preschian/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/preschian/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/preschian/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/preschian","id":734428,"login":"preschian","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczNDQyOA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/preschian/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/preschian/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/preschian/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/preschian/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/preschian/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/preschian","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chaotic-art/app/commits/3d5bc276dbbc2991a99bbbce64916001f4f58d35/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-19T06:59:20Z","email":"preschian@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Preschian Febryantara"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-19T06:59:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: switch on slow RPC with toast notifications (#789)\n\n* feat: switch on slow RPC with toast notifications\n\n- Add RPC provider switcher in navbar (icon button + popover with latency)\n- Add useRpcLatency composable (measureLatency, extractHostname, 1s threshold)\n- Add useRpcAutoSwitch: auto-switch to fastest RPC when current is slow\n- Toast when RPC slow: warn then success after switch\n- Refactor Settings RPC section to use shared useRpcLatency\n- Add AGENTS.md rule: always use English in code\n\nCloses #767\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* fix: remove duplicate toast initialization in useRpcAutoSwitch\n\n- Removed redundant toast initialization from the checkAndSwitch function.\n- Kept the toast initialization at the top of the useRpcAutoSwitch function for clarity.\n\n* refactor: enhance RPC provider handling in useRpcAutoSwitch\n\n- Introduced a type guard function to validate supported RPC providers.\n- Updated the type of lastAutoSwitchAt to better reflect its usage.\n- Reorganized toast notifications for clarity, ensuring a warning is shown when no faster provider is found.\n- Simplified the chain check in the watcher by utilizing the new type guard function.\n\n* refactor: consolidate latency handling in RpcProviderSwitcher and SettingsPage\n\n- Moved latencyColorClass and formatLatency functions to useRpcLatency composable for better reusability.\n- Updated RpcProviderSwitcher and SettingsPage components to utilize the new functions for latency display.\n- Cleaned up unused latency functions from components, enhancing code clarity and maintainability.\n\n* refactor: optimize latency measurement in RpcProviderSwitcher\n\n- Changed latencies from ref to shallowRef for improved performance.\n- Consolidated latency updates into a single Map to reduce unnecessary reactivity.\n- Triggered updates to latencies after measuring to ensure accurate state management.\n\n* refactor: enhance RPC provider display and auto-switch functionality\n\n- Introduced a computed property for chain name in RpcProviderSwitcher for improved readability.\n- Updated the toast notification logic in useRpcAutoSwitch to track the last auto-switch time for better state management.\n- Ensured consistent display of the current chain name in the UI.\n\n* refactor: improve RPC provider handling and latency management\n\n- Added a type guard function to validate supported chains in RpcProviderSwitcher.\n- Updated computed properties to ensure safe access to provider data based on chain support.\n- Changed latencies from ref to shallowRef in SettingsPage for better performance.\n- Triggered updates to latencies after measuring to maintain accurate state management.\n\n* refactor: streamline RPC provider management and enhance connection status display\n\n- Removed the RpcProviderSwitcher from the Navbar component for a cleaner layout.\n- Integrated the RpcProviderSwitcher into the default layout for consistent connection status visibility.\n- Implemented latency tracking and connection status updates in the RpcProviderSwitcher component.\n- Deleted the obsolete useRpcAutoSwitch composable and migrated its functionality to a new plugin for improved organization.\n- Updated the rpcProvider store to manage last measured latency for better user feedback on connection quality.\n\n* refactor: enhance RpcProviderSwitcher UI and improve latency display\n\n- Updated the RpcProviderSwitcher component to streamline the UI and improve the connection status display.\n- Refactored the template structure for better readability and maintainability.\n- Ensured consistent latency measurement feedback and improved user interaction with the RPC provider selection.\n- Adjusted type guard in rpcAutoSwitch plugin for better type safety.\n\n* refactor: optimize RPC provider selection and latency handling\n\n- Changed Promise.allSettled to Promise.all for improved latency measurement consistency.\n- Added a check to prevent selection of providers with errors in the RpcProviderSwitcher.\n- Enhanced the auto-switch logic to handle cases where all RPC providers are unreachable, providing user feedback through toast notifications.\n\n* refactor: enhance accessibility and latency handling in RPC components\n\n- Added aria-labels to buttons in RpcProviderSwitcher and SettingsPage for improved accessibility.\n- Updated DEFAULT_LATENCY_TIMEOUT_MS to 3000ms for better responsiveness in latency reporting.\n- Refined auto-switch logic in useRpcAutoSwitch to ensure clearer user feedback during provider checks.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"916b52b25d545fb3b1f1722ac30297755f0f962a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chaotic-art/app/git/trees/916b52b25d545fb3b1f1722ac30297755f0f962a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chaotic-art/app/git/commits/3d5bc276dbbc2991a99bbbce64916001f4f58d35","verification":{"payload":"tree 916b52b25d545fb3b1f1722ac30297755f0f962a\nparent 953df1c79d6f1c987cdfaa08201c8e4f470b7afc\nauthor Preschian Febryantara <preschian@users.noreply.github.com> 1771484360 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1771484360 +0700\n\nfeat: switch on slow RPC with toast notifications (#789)\n\n* feat: switch on slow RPC with toast notifications\n\n- Add RPC provider switcher in navbar (icon button + popover with latency)\n- Add useRpcLatency composable (measureLatency, extractHostname, 1s threshold)\n- Add useRpcAutoSwitch: auto-switch to fastest RPC when current is slow\n- Toast when RPC slow: warn then success after switch\n- Refactor Settings RPC section to use shared useRpcLatency\n- Add AGENTS.md rule: always use English in code\n\nCloses #767\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* fix: remove duplicate toast initialization in useRpcAutoSwitch\n\n- Removed redundant toast initialization from the checkAndSwitch function.\n- Kept the toast initialization at the top of the useRpcAutoSwitch function for clarity.\n\n* refactor: enhance RPC provider handling in useRpcAutoSwitch\n\n- Introduced a type guard function to validate supported RPC providers.\n- Updated the type of lastAutoSwitchAt to better reflect its usage.\n- Reorganized toast notifications for clarity, ensuring a warning is shown when no faster provider is found.\n- Simplified the chain check in the watcher by utilizing the new type guard function.\n\n* refactor: consolidate latency handling in RpcProviderSwitcher and SettingsPage\n\n- Moved latencyColorClass and formatLatency functions to useRpcLatency composable for better reusability.\n- Updated RpcProviderSwitcher and SettingsPage components to utilize the new functions for latency display.\n- Cleaned up unused latency functions from components, enhancing code clarity and maintainability.\n\n* refactor: optimize latency measurement in RpcProviderSwitcher\n\n- Changed latencies from ref to shallowRef for improved performance.\n- Consolidated latency updates into a single Map to reduce unnecessary reactivity.\n- Triggered updates to latencies after measuring to ensure accurate state management.\n\n* refactor: enhance RPC provider display and auto-switch functionality\n\n- Introduced a computed property for chain name in RpcProviderSwitcher for improved readability.\n- Updated the toast notification logic in useRpcAutoSwitch to track the last auto-switch time for better state management.\n- Ensured consistent display of the current chain name in the UI.\n\n* refactor: improve RPC provider handling and latency management\n\n- Added a type guard function to validate supported chains in RpcProviderSwitcher.\n- Updated computed properties to ensure safe access to provider data based on chain support.\n- Changed latencies from ref to shallowRef in SettingsPage for better performance.\n- Triggered updates to latencies after measuring to maintain accurate state management.\n\n* refactor: streamline RPC provider management and enhance connection status display\n\n- Removed the RpcProviderSwitcher from the Navbar component for a cleaner layout.\n- Integrated the RpcProviderSwitcher into the default layout for consistent connection status visibility.\n- Implemented latency tracking and connection status updates in the RpcProviderSwitcher component.\n- Deleted the obsolete useRpcAutoSwitch composable and migrated its functionality to a new plugin for improved organization.\n- Updated the rpcProvider store to manage last measured latency for better user feedback on connection quality.\n\n* refactor: enhance RpcProviderSwitcher UI and improve latency display\n\n- Updated the RpcProviderSwitcher component to streamline the UI and improve the connection status display.\n- Refactored the template structure for better readability and maintainability.\n- Ensured consistent latency measurement feedback and improved user interaction with the RPC provider selection.\n- Adjusted type guard in rpcAutoSwitch plugin for better type safety.\n\n* refactor: optimize RPC provider selection and latency handling\n\n- Changed Promise.allSettled to Promise.all for improved latency measurement consistency.\n- Added a check to prevent selection of providers with errors in the RpcProviderSwitcher.\n- Enhanced the auto-switch logic to handle cases where all RPC providers are unreachable, providing user feedback through toast notifications.\n\n* refactor: enhance accessibility and latency handling in RPC components\n\n- Added aria-labels to buttons in RpcProviderSwitcher and SettingsPage for improved accessibility.\n- Updated DEFAULT_LATENCY_TIMEOUT_MS to 3000ms for better responsiveness in latency reporting.\n- Refined auto-switch logic in useRpcAutoSwitch to ensure clearer user feedback during provider checks.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJplrTICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPngQAGdoMDZzqa+JbpjsZMYcV+Si\nUeDt3kR+g4gyVdfuQFvqvuqnSz69yVLfOqPytIxz52rpXd3vgiselF/Z7wlpvZfQ\ndnB7ctpmMTaCw2Xj6d6V1UElL2l+BVs8Rua9vMfAN+w/ZL737nbl4lJt7UMBoAzu\n2TsiUpgdHOBwMwUj+nvtJoSg62DsI0SgHwhLFichRZuafaoXXo+WIlvvhi3k/76x\nB4at52Z5SdpcS7VXLeGjl04/YLp6QSSDdtzbiyCnCu/UMlGA9AmASSoRLxWFp4mV\nnKE47sCqluWqDqrOv5+wjFEl3M7CZSTImSyaktA1DCLhFQ/3fiRwF1fb2PrLEoUI\noAx3w83+OkY6TO4snCxvVy6oYOgcIqiPAzm9QQwznl5vf+maAaju7bIUUTW2UBA/\nP1HGIGJqcDwYqvuIrhgo